# Trivy ignore file for the NEOTH repo.
#
# These advisories mirror `SRC/.cargo/audit.toml` and `SRC/deny.toml`.
# Each entry is unmaintained-only, has no safe upstream upgrade, or is
# unreachable from runtime input. The three files must change together.
#
# Re-evaluate per item when a safe upgrade lands upstream.

# bincode 1.x — WAL format-stable; v0.3 plans postcard migration.
RUSTSEC-2025-0141

# number_prefix — transitive via indicatif; upstream migration tracked.
RUSTSEC-2025-0119

# paste — archived, no vuln; transitive only; pastey migration pending upstream.
RUSTSEC-2024-0436

# xsalsa20poly1305 — transitive via peeroxide-dht; upstream bump tracked.
RUSTSEC-2023-0037

# serial 0.4.0 unmaintained — transitive via portable-pty; no vuln, only
# maintenance status. Upstream bump tracked.
RUSTSEC-2017-0008

# proc-macro-error2 — unmaintained; transitive through Matrix/vodozemac.
RUSTSEC-2026-0173

# rustls-pemfile — unmaintained; transitive through the IRC adapter.
RUSTSEC-2025-0134

# ttf-parser and rustybuzz — unmaintained (not vulnerable), with no compatible
# safe upgrade in the current Slint/usvg and lopdf stacks. Upstream migrations
# to skrifa/harfrust are re-evaluated for every release.
RUSTSEC-2026-0192
RUSTSEC-2026-0206

# rsa Marvin timing side-channel — no upstream patch; only used by the local
# outbound SSH client, matching the advisory's documented safe-use case.
RUSTSEC-2023-0071

# quick-xml <0.41 remains only in wayland-scanner's build-time proc macro over
# vendored protocol XML. Runtime parsers resolve to the fixed 0.41 line.
RUSTSEC-2026-0194
RUSTSEC-2026-0195
